---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'How to Apply for China Tourist Visa (L-Type) 2026: A Step-by-Step Guide';
const description = 'Complete step-by-step guide for applying to a Chinese L-type tourist visa in 2026. Official documents, COVA online form, appointment booking, fees, and FAQ.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-12">
      <a href="/en/prepare/visa/" class="text-sm text-brand-600 hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1 mb-4">← Visa & Entry</a>
      <div class="text-sm text-brand-600 font-medium tracking-wide uppercase mb-3">Tourist Visa</div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight mb-4">
        How to Apply for China Tourist Visa (L-Type) 2026: A Step-by-Step Guide
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8 not-prose">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-1"><strong>Official portals:</strong></p>
        <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li>📋 <a href="http://cova.mfa.gov.cn/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">COVA Online Form</a> — Fill in your visa application</li>
          <li>📖 <a href="https://consular.mfa.gov.cn/VISA/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Consular Affairs Visa Guide</a> — Official step-by-step guidance</li>
          <li>📍 <a href="https://www.visaforchina.cn" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visa Application Centers</a> — Find your local center & book appointments</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        If you've read our <a href="/en/prepare/visa/visa-guide/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">China Visa Types Complete Guide</a> and confirmed you need an L-type tourist visa — here's exactly how to apply, step by step, using the official online system.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Do You Need an L-Type Visa?</h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-4">
        <strong>You need an L-type tourist visa if:</strong>
      </p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 mb-6">
        <li>Your passport is NOT from one of the <a href="/en/prepare/visa/visa-free/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">50 visa-free countries</a></li>
        <li>You do NOT have a qualifying third-country itinerary for <a href="/en/prepare/visa/transit-240/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">240-hour transit</a></li>
        <li>You plan to visit China for tourism (not work, study, or business)</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
        L-type visas are typically issued for 30, 60, or 90 days per entry. Multiple-entry options are available depending on your nationality and visa history.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">What Documents Do You Need?</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Based on the <a href="https://cs.mfa.gov.cn/wgrlh/lhqz/cjwdn_660600/201407/t20140717_961493.shtml" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official Chinese Consular Affairs Website</a>, here's what you must prepare:
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Basic Documents (Everyone)</h3>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-8 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left">
          <thead class="bg-gray-50">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Document</th>
              <th class="px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Requirement</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Valid passport</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">At least 6 months validity remaining, with at least 2 blank visa pages</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Visa application form</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Completed online via <a href="http://cova.mfa.gov.cn/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">COVA system</a>, then printed and signed by hand</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Passport photo</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">1 recent color photo — 48mm × 33mm, white background</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Previous Chinese visa (if any)</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Photocopy of your last Chinese visa (if you had one)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Proof of legal stay</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Residence permit or visa for your current country (if applying outside your home country)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Supporting Documents</h3>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Choose <strong>one</strong> of the following:</p>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-5 mb-4 not-prose">
        <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Option A — Independent Travel</p>
        <ul class="text-sm text-gray-700 space-y-1 list-disc pl-4">
          <li>Round-trip flight booking (reservation is fine — don't buy tickets before visa approval)</li>
          <li>Hotel reservations for your entire stay</li>
          <li>A rough itinerary showing which cities you plan to visit</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-5 mb-6 not-prose">
        <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Option B — Invitation Letter</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-2">An invitation letter from a Chinese citizen or a foreigner with a Chinese residence permit. It must include:</p>
        <ul class="text-sm text-gray-700 space-y-1 list-disc pl-4">
          <li>Your personal info (name, gender, date of birth, passport number)</li>
          <li>Your travel details (arrival/departure dates, places you'll visit)</li>
          <li>The inviter's info (name, phone number, address, signature)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-4 mb-6 not-prose">
        <p class="text-sm text-amber-800 flex items-start gap-2">
          <span class="font-bold">Note:</span> The consular officer may request additional documents or an in-person interview if needed, depending on your specific situation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Photo Requirements</h2>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-8 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left">
          <thead class="bg-gray-50">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Specification</th>
              <th class="px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Requirement</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Size</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">48mm x 33mm</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Background</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Plain white</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Recency</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Taken within the last 6 months</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Expression</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Neutral, mouth closed, both eyes visible</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Glasses</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">No glasses, sunglasses, or tinted lenses</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Retouching</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">No Photoshop, no filters, no heavy editing</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">Many visa centers offer on-site photo services if you're worried yours won't pass the requirements.</p>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Step-by-Step Application Process</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Step 1: Fill Out the COVA Form</h3>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Go to the official <a href="http://cova.mfa.gov.cn/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">COVA system (cova.mfa.gov.cn)</a> and complete the visa application form online. COVA is a form-filling tool — once you submit it online, you'll need to print the completed form and bring it to the visa center in person. It's not an online submission system; the physical paper form is what the visa officer actually processes.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Have these ready before you start:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-gray-700 mb-4">
        <li>Your passport (number, issue date, expiry date)</li>
        <li>Your employer or school name and address</li>
        <li>Your planned entry and exit dates</li>
        <li>A rough idea of cities you'll visit</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        <strong>Important:</strong> After filling out the form, download and print it. You must sign it by hand before bringing it to the visa center. Without the printed and signed form, the visa center won't accept your application.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Step 2: Book an Appointment</h3>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        After submitting the COVA form, visit the <a href="https://www.visaforchina.cn" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">China Visa Application Service Center website</a> to book an appointment.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">During booking:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-gray-700 mb-4">
        <li>Select <strong>"Tourist Visa (L)"</strong> as the visa type</li>
        <li>Choose your nearest center — each center covers specific regions</li>
        <li>Pick an available date and time slot</li>
        <li>You'll get a confirmation email with a QR code — save it</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-xl p-4 mb-6 not-prose">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
          <strong>Can't find an appointment?</strong> Some centers accept walk-ins, usually early in the morning. Check your local center's policy on their website.
        </p>
      </div>

      <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Step 3: Visit the Visa Center</h3>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Bring <strong>all your documents</strong> to the visa center on your appointment day.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">What happens once you're inside:</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 mb-4">
        <li><strong>Security check</strong> — Your bag goes through an X-ray machine, similar to airport security</li>
        <li><strong>Document review</strong> — A staff member checks your documents before you queue</li>
        <li><strong>Biometrics</strong> — They'll scan your fingerprints (usually both index fingers)</li>
        <li><strong>Photo</strong> — They may take a new photo on-site (so don't stress too much about your own photo)</li>
        <li><strong>Payment</strong> — Pay the visa fee (cash, card, or money order, depending on the center)</li>
      </ol>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        The in-person part usually takes <strong>30-60 minutes</strong> depending on the queue.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Step 4: Wait for Processing</h3>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 mb-4">
        <li><strong>Standard processing:</strong> 4-5 business days (most locations)</li>
        <li><strong>Express service:</strong> 2-3 business days (extra fee)</li>
        <li><strong>Rush service:</strong> 1 business day (available at some locations, premium fee)</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">

      <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Step 5: Pick Up Your Passport</h3>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Return to the visa center with your pickup receipt.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Check your visa immediately before leaving:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-gray-700 mb-6">
        <li>Is the visa type labeled <strong>"L"</strong>?</li>
        <li>Are the validity dates correct?</li>
        <li>Is the number of entries correct (single vs. multiple)?</li>
        <li>Is your name spelled correctly?</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
        If anything is wrong, tell them <strong>before you leave</strong>.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Official Links</h2>

      <table class="w-full mb-8">
        <thead class="bg-gray-50">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 text-left">Resource</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 text-left">Link</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 text-left">Purpose</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">COVA Online Form</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm"><a href="http://cova.mfa.gov.cn/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cova.mfa.gov.cn</a></td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Complete your visa application form online</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Consular Visa Guide</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm"><a href="https://consular.mfa.gov.cn/VISA/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">consular.mfa.gov.cn/VISA/</a></td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Official step-by-step guidance from the Chinese government</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Visa Centers</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm"><a href="https://www.visaforchina.cn" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">visaforchina.cn</a></td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Find your nearest center and book appointments</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 font-medium">Consular Affairs</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm"><a href="https://cs.mfa.gov.cn/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cs.mfa.gov.cn</a></td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700">Official requirements, FAQs, and policy updates</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">FAQ — L-Type Tourist Visa</h2>

      <div class="space-y-6 mb-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How much does a Chinese tourist visa cost?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Fees vary by nationality and number of entries. For US citizens, a single-entry L visa costs around <strong>$140 USD</strong>. For EU and UK citizens, expect roughly <strong>£85-£170</strong> depending on the center. Check your local visa center's fee schedule for the exact amount.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can I get a multiple-entry L visa?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Yes, if you've had a Chinese visa before (any type), you're more likely to be approved for multiple entries. First-time applicants typically receive single-entry visas.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How early should I apply?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Apply <strong>1-3 months</strong> before your trip. Don't apply too early (visas have limited validity periods) but don't leave it to the last minute either. The visa center website will tell you the earliest date you can submit.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can I extend my L visa once I'm in China?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Extensions are possible but not guaranteed. You'd need to visit the local Public Security Bureau (PSB) Entry-Exit Administration office. It's easier to request a longer duration (60 or 90 days) during your initial application.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
      </div>

      <hr class="my-10 border-gray-200" />

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Before applying for a visa, check whether you qualify for <a href="/en/prepare/visa/visa-free/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">visa-free entry</a> or the <a href="/en/prepare/visa/transit-240/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">240-hour transit policy</a>. If not, the L-type tourist visa is the standard route for visitors coming to China.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
        *Last updated: June 2026. Always check the <a href="https://cs.mfa.gov.cn/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">official consular website</a> for the latest requirements.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
